      "changes": 6,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs_new%2Fdocs%2Fget-started%2Fquickstart.mdx?ref=368e08de93a7038d0a67884178a4262fd13e3c93",
      "deletions": 3,
      "filename": "docs_new/docs/get-started/quickstart.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ pip install -e \"python\"\n         --env \"HF_TOKEN=<secret>\" \\\n         --ipc=host \\\n         lmsysorg/sglang:latest \\\n-        python3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000\n+        sglang serve --model-path meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000\n     ```\n \n     For production deployments, use the smaller **runtime** variant (~40% size reduction):\n@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ pip install -e \"python\"\n         --env \"HF_TOKEN=<secret>\" \\\n         --ipc=host \\\n         lmsysorg/sglang:latest-runtime \\\n-        python3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000\n+        sglang serve --model-path meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000\n     ```\n   </Tab>\n </Tabs>\n@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@ export CUDA_HOME=/usr/local/cuda-<your-cuda-version>\n Start the SGLang server with a model. Here we use `qwen/qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct` as a lightweight example:\n \n ```bash\n-python3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path qwen/qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000\n+sglang serve --model-path qwen/qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000\n ```\n \n Wait until you see `The server is fired up and ready to roll!` in the terminal output.",
